Count only boot progress against the first-boot idle timeout.

The hostagent repeats its last status with every port forwarding and vsock
event, so treating every event as progress kept the idle timeout from ever
firing while cloud-init progress was missing. A wait that a deadline ends
before cloud-init reports completion is now an error, not a ready VM.

